      "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this chapter we verify basic properties of moduli spaces\nand moduli stacks such as\n<MATH_0001>, <MATH_0002>, <MATH_0003>,\n<MATH_0004>, <MATH_0005>,\n<MATH_0006>, <MATH_0007>, <MATH_0008>,\n<MATH_0009>, <MATH_0010>, and\n<MATH_0011>.\nWe have already shown these algebraic spaces or algebraic stacks\nunder suitable hypotheses, see Quot, Sections\n<REF_0001>,\n<REF_0002>,\n<REF_0003>,\n<REF_0004>,\n<REF_0005>,\n<REF_0006>,\n<REF_0007>,\n<REF_0008>,\n<REF_0009>,\n<REF_0010>,\n<REF_0011>, and\n<REF_0012>.\nThe stack of curves, denoted <MATH_0012> and introduced\nin Quot, Section <REF_0013>, is discussed in the\nchapter on moduli of curves, see\nModuli of Curves, Section <REF_0014>.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nIn some sense this chapter is following the footsteps of\nGrothendieck's lectures <REF_0015>,\n<REF_0016>,\n<REF_0017>,\n<REF_0018>,\n<REF_0019>, and\n<REF_0020>.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
      "source_text_hash": "sha256:6a4500f167a877f093e6d7f0ed2bd89b72566e6438f9e73b4929ac33228e65a8",
      "unit_id": "tag:0DLU:prose-0001"
    }
